# Which Is Bigger? — Numbers
# answer-mode: choice

More: trees on Earth, or stars in the Milky Way?
---
Trees on Earth
~ Stars in the Milky Way
---
About 3 trillion trees vs 100–400 billion stars. Roughly ten trees for every star.

More: atoms in a glass of water, or glasses of water in all Earth's oceans?
---
Atoms in a glass of water
~ Glasses of water in all Earth's oceans
---
~10²⁵ atoms in one glass vs ~5×10²¹ glassfuls in every ocean. The atoms win by a few thousand times.

More: neurons in one human brain, or people on Earth?
---
Neurons in one human brain
~ People on Earth
---
~86 billion neurons vs ~8 billion people. Ten brains' worth of people, or one brain outnumbers humanity ten to one.

Heavier: all humans on Earth combined, or all ants on Earth combined?
---
All humans on Earth combined
~ All ants on Earth combined
---
Roughly five to one: ~60 megatonnes of human carbon vs ~12 for the world's ~20 quadrillion ants. The old claim that ants outweigh us didn't survive the 2022 ant census.

Longer: a day on Venus, or a year on Venus?
---
A day on Venus
~ A year on Venus
---
One rotation takes 243 Earth days; one orbit takes 225. And it spins backwards.

More: possible chess games, or atoms in the observable universe?
---
Possible chess games
~ Atoms in the observable universe
---
~10¹²⁰ games (the Shannon number) vs ~10⁸⁰ atoms. Not even close.

More: ways to shuffle a deck of 52 cards, or seconds since the Big Bang?
---
Ways to shuffle a deck of 52 cards
~ Seconds since the Big Bang
---
52! ≈ 8×10⁶⁷ orderings vs ~4×10¹⁷ seconds. Any well-shuffled deck is almost certainly in an order no deck has ever been in.

More: stars in the observable universe, or grains of sand on all Earth's beaches?
---
Stars in the observable universe
~ Grains of sand on all Earth's beaches
---
~10²² or more stars vs ~10¹⁹ grains — a thousand-plus stars per grain of beach sand.

Bigger time gap: Stegosaurus to T. rex, or T. rex to today?
---
Stegosaurus to T. rex
~ T. rex to today
---
Stegosaurus died out ~150 million years ago, T. rex lived ~68–66 million years ago: an ~80-million-year gap vs 66. T. rex is closer to your phone than to a Stegosaurus.

Bigger time gap: the Great Pyramid to Cleopatra, or Cleopatra to the Moon landing?
---
The Great Pyramid to Cleopatra
~ Cleopatra to the Moon landing
---
Pyramid ~2560 BC, Cleopatra died 30 BC, Apollo 11 in 1969: ~2,530 years vs ~2,000.

Heavier: a blue whale's heart, or an adult human?
---
A blue whale's heart
~ An adult human
---
~180 kg vs ~70 kg. Golf-cart sized, not car-sized — the car myth died when one was actually weighed in 2015.

More pizza: one 18-inch pizza, or two 12-inch pizzas?
---
One 18-inch pizza
~ Two 12-inch pizzas
---
Area grows with the radius squared: 254 vs 226 square inches. One big pizza beats two mediums.

Taller: the Eiffel Tower in summer, or in winter?
---
The Eiffel Tower in summer
~ The Eiffel Tower in winter
---
Thermal expansion of the iron adds up to ~15 cm on a hot day.
